          "ImageDescription": {
            "value": "Town entrance sign, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lochiel,_South_Australia\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:Lochiel, South Australia\">Lochiel, South Australia</a>. Lochiel is adjacent to <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lake_Bumbunga\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:Lake Bumbunga\">Lake Bumbunga</a>, where salt is harvested. The horses depicted are pulling a \"salt scrape\" used in early days; the top area represents the hills on the side of the lake and the middle shows the pink colour of the water. The low wall at the front has a representation of a humorous sculpture in the lake, \"Loch Eel\", which is visible from the northern approaches to the township.",
            "source": "commons-desc-page"
          },
